    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully tested against every requirement.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `src/server.js` — Express 5.3.0 app with all four routes, validation, and JSON error handling\n- `src/db.js` — `pg` connection pool reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment\n- `src/migrate.js` + `migrations/001_create_links.sql` — migration runner tracking applied migrations in a `schema_migrations` table\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (verified via kernel listen entry; no npm install inside)\n- `README.md` — startup instructions and API docs\n\n**Verified end-to-end:**\n- `POST /links` → 201 with unchanged URL; generated codes (8-char random) when omitted; 409 on duplicate custom code; 422 for malformed JSON, missing/relative/ftp URLs, bad codes (too short/long, bad chars, non-string)\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 / 404; `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with exact `Location` header and atomic one-per-request click increment (2 redirects → clicks 2); `GET /links` → ascending order with `total`\n- Restart test: killed and relaunched via `sh start.sh` — all links and click counts persisted, migration correctly skipped as already applied"
  }
